WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:31.125
In the previous few verses,

2
00:00:31.125 --> 00:00:33.958
Lord Krishna has instructed 
Arjuna about turning inward

3
00:00:33.958 --> 00:00:37.583
to attain inner happiness.

4
00:00:37.583 --> 00:00:38.833
Now in this verse,

5
00:00:38.833 --> 00:00:41.875
he describes the qualities of a person

6
00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:44.583
who has become free from all illusions

7
00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:45.833
of material world

8
00:00:45.833 --> 00:00:46.666
and is advancing

9
00:00:46.666 --> 00:00:49.666
on the path of spiritual progress.

10
00:00:54.708 --> 00:00:55.875
How does a person

11
00:00:55.875 --> 00:00:58.291
who has become free 
from material attachments

12
00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.583
work for the benefit of this

13
00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:02.916
creation and other beings?

14
00:01:02.916 --> 00:01:04.416
Lord Krishna answers this question

15
00:01:04.416 --> 00:01:06.083
in this verse.

16
00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:07.291
He says,

17
00:01:07.291 --> 00:01:09.750
such people rise above opposing states like

18
00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.541
happiness-sorrow, success-failure 
by freeing themselves

19
00:01:13.541 --> 00:01:16.583
from the illusory cycle of the material world.

20
00:01:16.583 --> 00:01:19.291
They attain such inner balance

21
00:01:19.291 --> 00:01:22.541
that remains unaffected by life's ups and downs.

22
00:01:22.541 --> 00:01:25.541
But such wise ones don't 
just abandon the material world

23
00:01:25.541 --> 00:01:28.583
to remain absorbed in their spiritual bliss,

24
00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:30.083
rather, they remain eager for the welfare

25
00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:32.875
of the entire creation.

26
00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:35.541
They don't renounce worldly relationships,

27
00:01:35.541 --> 00:01:37.583
but illuminate the entire 
creation with their knowledge

28
00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:39.916
and compassion.

29
00:01:39.916 --> 00:01:41.250
In their view, every being

30
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.375
is but a part of the Supreme.

31
00:01:43.375 --> 00:01:44.583
They dedicate their lives

32
00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:47.416
for the welfare of all beings,

33
00:01:47.416 --> 00:01:49.250
and with each of their actions,

34
00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:52.875
they try to connect others to this truth.

35
00:01:52.875 --> 00:01:54.333
Lord Krishna explains

36
00:01:54.333 --> 00:01:55.375
that such people are not

37
00:01:55.375 --> 00:01:57.416
only free from sins,

38
00:01:57.416 --> 00:01:58.666
but also have no duality

39
00:01:58.666 --> 00:02:00.416
in their minds.

40
00:02:00.416 --> 00:02:02.500
They neither harbor feelings like anger,

41
00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.291
greed, and craving towards anyone,

42
00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.750
nor do they feel pride in any achievement, nor

43
00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.708
sorrow in any failure.

44
00:02:10.708 --> 00:02:11.375
Their mind

45
00:02:11.375 --> 00:02:14.458
remains completely stable and balanced.

46
00:02:14.458 --> 00:02:17.083
This state enables them to
 make appropriate

47
00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:20.083
decisions in every situation.

48
00:02:20.083 --> 00:02:22.625
Eventually, such people attain Brahma-nirvana,

49
00:02:22.625 --> 00:02:23.208
meaning

50
00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:26.458
the realization of the Supreme.

51
00:02:26.458 --> 00:02:27.875
Lord Krishna says

52
00:02:27.875 --> 00:02:29.958
that this path is certainly difficult,

53
00:02:29.958 --> 00:02:32.083
but not impossible.

54
00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:35.125
This divine achievement can be
 attained through self-purification,

55
00:02:35.125 --> 00:02:38.458
self-reflection, and a spirit of altruism.

56
00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:39.875
This is the path

57
00:02:39.875 --> 00:02:42.708
that not only frees a person from all

58
00:02:42.708 --> 00:02:44.083
sorrows,

59
00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:44.916
but also opens

60
00:02:44.916 --> 00:02:48.791
the door to the welfare of the entire creation.

61
00:02:53.625 --> 00:02:54.458
Is it appropriate

62
00:02:54.458 --> 00:02:57.750
to completely dedicate yourself

63
00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:00.916
to helping others

64
00:03:00.916 --> 00:03:07.916
and not think about yourself?

65
00:03:07.916 --> 00:03:15.833
In your lifetime, you must have helped 
someone or the other at some point.

66
00:03:15.833 --> 00:03:19.666
Whether it's supporting a friend,

67
00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:23.208
taking care of your family,

68
00:03:23.208 --> 00:03:26.750
or taking on responsibilities for some work,

69
00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:31.125
and this nature of yours is commendable.

70
00:03:31.125 --> 00:03:33.083
Those who have truly

71
00:03:33.083 --> 00:03:35.333
reached the level of self-realization

72
00:03:35.333 --> 00:03:42.583
always work for the welfare of all beings.

73
00:03:42.583 --> 00:03:44.541
However,

74
00:03:44.541 --> 00:03:50.333
if you forget yourself while helping others

75
00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:57.125
and don't pay attention to 
your physical and mental health,

76
00:03:57.125 --> 00:03:59.416
then fatigue,

77
00:03:59.416 --> 00:04:02.166
stress,

78
00:04:02.166 --> 00:04:05.750
and dissatisfaction begin to develop within you.

79
00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:12.250
And then, you cannot properly help anyone.

80
00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:14.375
Imagine

81
00:04:14.375 --> 00:04:16.291
that you've jumped into water

82
00:04:16.291 --> 00:04:19.916
to save a drowning person,

83
00:04:19.916 --> 00:04:21.458
but if

84
00:04:21.458 --> 00:04:23.708
you don't know how to swim

85
00:04:23.708 --> 00:04:27.208
and are drowning yourself,

86
00:04:27.208 --> 00:04:31.125
then will you be able to save that person?

87
00:04:31.125 --> 00:04:32.583
No!

88
00:04:32.583 --> 00:04:34.541
Similarly,

89
00:04:34.541 --> 00:04:38.666
if you're giving your time and energy to others,

90
00:04:38.666 --> 00:04:41.083
without nourishing yourself mentally,

91
00:04:41.083 --> 00:04:45.541
emotionally, and spiritually,

92
00:04:45.541 --> 00:04:49.208
then you will experience fatigue

93
00:04:49.208 --> 00:04:51.625
and disappointment within yourself,

94
00:04:51.625 --> 00:04:54.083
and won't be able to help others

95
00:04:54.083 --> 00:04:57.208
properly.

96
00:04:57.208 --> 00:04:59.250
Remember,

97
00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:03.458
taking care of yourself is not selfishness,

98
00:05:03.458 --> 00:05:06.250
it's a necessity.

99
00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:09.083
When you connect with your inner peace

100
00:05:09.083 --> 00:05:11.500
and balance,

101
00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:15.125
your capacity to help others increases

102
00:05:15.125 --> 00:05:19.458
manifold.

103
00:05:19.458 --> 00:05:22.666
You can serve others without getting tired

104
00:05:22.666 --> 00:05:26.083
and without negativity,

105
00:05:26.083 --> 00:05:27.833
and your actions arise

106
00:05:27.833 --> 00:05:31.791
from love and compassion.

107
00:05:36.458 --> 00:05:38.500
Is it inappropriate

108
00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:46.958
to be strict for the benefit of a
 family member or a loved one?

109
00:05:46.958 --> 00:05:49.875
Compassion is a great virtue,

110
00:05:49.875 --> 00:05:54.625
considered the highest virtue in society.

111
00:05:54.625 --> 00:05:55.666
Compassion

112
00:05:55.666 --> 00:05:57.208
works like light

113
00:05:57.208 --> 00:06:00.750
in someone's life.

114
00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:05.541
When you show compassion towards others,

115
00:06:05.541 --> 00:06:09.666
it gives them confidence,

116
00:06:09.666 --> 00:06:13.791
affection, strength, and 
support during difficult times.

117
00:06:13.791 --> 00:06:17.166
The purpose of true 
compassion should always be

118
00:06:17.166 --> 00:06:23.458
to guide others towards a positive path.

119
00:06:23.458 --> 00:06:25.500
If your compassion encourages someone's

120
00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:29.375
harmful behavior or

121
00:06:29.375 --> 00:06:30.458
encourages them

122
00:06:30.458 --> 00:06:34.791
to walk on the path of destruction,

123
00:06:34.791 --> 00:06:38.625
then it becomes more harmful.

124
00:06:38.625 --> 00:06:40.541
Imagine

125
00:06:40.541 --> 00:06:43.625
if a loved one is

126
00:06:43.625 --> 00:06:45.333
caught in some addiction

127
00:06:45.333 --> 00:06:48.708
or abusive behavior,

128
00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:50.541
naturally,

129
00:06:50.541 --> 00:06:53.458
you would want to help them.

130
00:06:53.458 --> 00:06:56.083
But sometimes

131
00:06:56.083 --> 00:06:59.791
this compassionate feeling

132
00:06:59.791 --> 00:07:04.333
becomes a kind of convenience for them.

133
00:07:04.333 --> 00:07:07.666
When you ignore their behavior

134
00:07:07.666 --> 00:07:12.583
or provide them with resources

135
00:07:12.583 --> 00:07:17.500
that encourage their tendency,

136
00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.083
then this compassion,

137
00:07:19.083 --> 00:07:22.375
which seems helpful for a moment,

138
00:07:22.375 --> 00:07:23.166
actually

139
00:07:23.166 --> 00:07:27.541
pushes them in an inappropriate direction.

140
00:07:27.541 --> 00:07:28.708
It prevents them

141
00:07:28.708 --> 00:07:29.750
from facing the consequences

142
00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:32.500
of their actions,

143
00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:37.291
and making necessary changes in their lives.

144
00:07:37.291 --> 00:07:41.875
True compassion leads others
 towards welfare, self-development,

145
00:07:41.875 --> 00:07:45.583
and self-realization.

146
00:07:45.583 --> 00:07:46.458
Many times,

147
00:07:46.458 --> 00:07:51.083
you'll have to be strict to help someone.

148
00:07:51.083 --> 00:07:53.291
You'll have to encourage them to reach 

149
00:07:53.291 --> 00:07:56.666
their true potential,

150
00:07:56.666 --> 00:07:59.666
and provide guidance

151
00:07:59.666 --> 00:08:03.583
that will lead them towards their improvement.

152
00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:08.583
Compassion doesn't mean just avoiding 
discomfort or struggle,

153
00:08:08.583 --> 00:08:10.416
but it means

154
00:08:10.416 --> 00:08:15.500
that we make necessary decisions 
to show others the right path,

155
00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:18.666
even if it's difficult.

156
00:08:18.666 --> 00:08:22.791
The true form of love and compassion is that

157
00:08:22.791 --> 00:08:26.333
which lifts someone up in life, not

158
00:08:26.333 --> 00:08:30.458
lets them fall deeper into darkness.

159
00:08:35.208 --> 00:08:37.541
In the professional world,

160
00:08:37.541 --> 00:08:40.333
the desire to help others is natural,

161
00:08:40.333 --> 00:08:44.833
especially when you are in the role of a leader or

162
00:08:44.833 --> 00:08:48.625
a guide.

163
00:08:48.625 --> 00:08:51.708
Generally, you think

164
00:08:51.708 --> 00:08:54.541
that you should help others 
by solving 

165
00:08:54.541 --> 00:08:57.625
their problems yourself,

166
00:08:57.625 --> 00:09:02.125
thinking that it is in their best interest.

167
00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:03.916
But,

168
00:09:03.916 --> 00:09:06.083
do you know,

169
00:09:06.083 --> 00:09:08.083
real help isn't just

170
00:09:08.083 --> 00:09:11.250
in solving someone's problems,

171
00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:14.750
but in giving them proper guidance,

172
00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:19.541
knowledge, skills, and confidence,

173
00:09:19.541 --> 00:09:20.416
so

174
00:09:20.416 --> 00:09:23.833
they can solve their problems themselves,

175
00:09:23.833 --> 00:09:26.875
and not remain dependent on anyone.

176
00:09:26.875 --> 00:09:28.958
Imagine you are

177
00:09:28.958 --> 00:09:32.791
the head of an organization,

178
00:09:32.791 --> 00:09:35.333
and you complete difficult tasks

179
00:09:35.333 --> 00:09:38.333
of your organization yourself.

180
00:09:38.333 --> 00:09:41.416
Perhaps it might seem 
beneficial to other members

181
00:09:41.416 --> 00:09:45.625
of the organization for some time,

182
00:09:45.625 --> 00:09:47.416
but

183
00:09:47.416 --> 00:09:50.708
this won't increase their knowledge.

184
00:09:50.708 --> 00:09:55.625
And gradually, they will become completely

185
00:09:55.625 --> 00:09:59.333
dependent on you, and will be unable to solve

186
00:09:59.333 --> 00:10:05.083
any problem in the future.

187
00:10:05.083 --> 00:10:08.916
In this way, while helping others,

188
00:10:08.916 --> 00:10:12.833
you teach them to depend on others,

189
00:10:12.833 --> 00:10:16.541
which is not suitable for their development.

190
00:10:16.541 --> 00:10:19.916
But successful leadership is that

191
00:10:19.916 --> 00:10:24.208
which enables the members of the 
organization by giving them proper guidance,

192
00:10:24.208 --> 00:10:30.416
knowledge, skills, and confidence.

193
00:10:30.416 --> 00:10:33.750
It prepares colleagues

194
00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:38.291
for future problems by 
not giving immediate solutions.

195
00:10:38.291 --> 00:10:41.833
Become like a coach,

196
00:10:41.833 --> 00:10:43.458
just as a coach

197
00:10:43.458 --> 00:10:47.166
doesn't start playing on the field himself,

198
00:10:47.166 --> 00:10:49.916
but enables players to think

199
00:10:49.916 --> 00:10:53.250
and make decisions,

200
00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.958
so that they can adapt 
themselves to any situation

201
00:10:55.958 --> 00:10:59.500
during the game

202
00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:01.083
and become victorious.

203
00:11:01.083 --> 00:11:03.500
Compassion in the workplace

204
00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:07.541
doesn't just mean helping colleagues,

205
00:11:07.541 --> 00:11:11.583
but making them self-reliant.

206
00:11:11.583 --> 00:11:14.833
When you enable them to think, make decisions,

207
00:11:14.833 --> 00:11:20.083
and solve any problem,

208
00:11:20.083 --> 00:11:23.750
then you are truly helping them.

209
00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:25.375
True leadership

210
00:11:25.375 --> 00:11:29.208
enables its organization in such a way

211
00:11:29.208 --> 00:11:33.333
that they can solve their own problems,

212
00:11:33.333 --> 00:11:37.666
not remain excessively dependent on anyone!
